        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Dunrobin Gin is a Highland craft gin made in Golspie, in the Scottish Highlands. Lizzie and Boban created it to evoke the experience of forest and garden, using leaves and roots gathered around Dunrobin Castle, where the woodland meets the sea. It brings home in a bottle the feeling of standing in the garden after the rain, breathing it all in.</p><p>The recipe has a base of juniper, coriander seed and angelica root. Lemon, rose-scented pelargonium leaf and blackcurrant leaf add lighter tones, and a light touch of clove brings a hint of warmth, with spring water from the Big Burn. It is bottled at 45% ABV in a 70cl bottle and sealed by hand in green wax.</p><p>Every bottle carries <em>Sans Peur</em>, “without fear”, the motto of the House of Sutherland. Order it here, or find it at the <a href=\"/pages/visit\">Wee Gin Shop at Dunrobin Castle</a>.</p>"
          }
